  "description": "Tidal saltworks on a late-afternoon marsh: brine pans, salt crust, timber and tar on the quay, copper only as a small accent. Dim brine-tinted light and coloured fog keep the saturated colours from blowing out.",
  "provenance": {
    "derivation": "external-reference",
    "authoredBy": "presentation",
    "authoredAt": "2026-10-13",
    "note": "Palette sRGB values are the authored Config.colors roles for the saltworks, recorded here as art direction. They were not measured from a built Saltmere place, and no value in this file was taken from a candidate capture. Lighting budgets follow the platform rendering notes: brightness stays at 1.7 and ambient stays dim, because high brightness plus high ambient blows saturated colour out.",
    "references": [
      {
        "id": "saltmere-design-presentation",
        "kind": "document",
        "note": "games/saltmere/DESIGN.md Presentation: late-afternoon marsh, low brightness, coloured fog, few lights. A design contract, not a measurement of a built place."
      },
      {
        "id": "config-colors",
        "kind": "specification",
        "note": "sRGB triples are the authored Config.colors values (brine, salt, timber, tar, copper, marsh, foam, stone). They were not measured from this game."
      },
      {
        "id": "engine-facts-rendering",
        "kind": "document",
        "note": "docs/platform/ENGINE-FACTS.md rendering: high brightness plus high ambient blows saturated colour out; few point lights; neon stacks."
      }
    ]
  },
